What: host2ansible
Command: host2ansible
How it's going to work:

host2ansible is going to ssh to hosts and first identify:
	1. Red Hat, Rocky
	2. Debian

Once identified, it will look for configuration in known places for:

	1. system
	2. security
	3. services
	4. firewall

The system will specialize in:
	
	1. nginx
	2. postfix
	3. apache
	4. docker
	5. k3s
	6. postgres
	7. pgbouncer / pgdog / pgcat as necessary
	8. firewall configuration
	8a. can we run this through our ~/development/fweng system?

After analyzing all of this, it will then look for monitoring services, our own services, our own tools

Then after all of this is collected, it is going to write a: <hostname>/<service> or just <hostname> or <container> directory with:
	1. the configuration
	2. run_converted.py -- a ihat runs the converted item
	   2a. should have test and validation features 
	   2b. the executation part
	   2c. validation post execution

This is what the world needs.

